      "text": "In the paper by **Morettini et al. (2022)**, the numerical values for the **fasting (basal) amino acid concentration ($AA_b$)** are shared indirectly through the validation dataset cited from **Karusheva et al. (2019)**.\n\nWhile the paper focuses on the estimated kinetic parameters ($k_{GL}$, $k_{AA}$), it provides the following information regarding fasting levels:\n\n### **1. Fasting Amino Acid Values ($AA_b$)**\nThe study uses **Branched-Chain Amino Acids (BCAAs)**—specifically the sum of Leucine, Isoleucine, and Valine—as the representative \"amino acids\" for Model 1. The basal values used for the model validation (from the average experimental data in Figure 3) are approximately:\n*   **Control (CNT):** ~470 $\\mu$mol/L\n*   **Type 2 Diabetes (T2D):** ~530 $\\mu$mol/L\n\nThese values correspond to the $t \u003d 0$ (fasting) data points shown in **Figure 3, Panel C** of the paper (titled \"BCAA curves from the reference mean experimental data\").\n\n### **2. Role in Model 1 Calculations**\nThe fasting amino acid value ($AA_b$) is a critical component for calculating the **Basal Insulin Appearance Rate ($BR_I$)**. As described on **Page 3** of the PDF, the paper uses the following formula to ensure the system is at steady state at $t\u003d0$:\n$$BR_I \u003d k_I \\cdot I_b - k_{GL} \\cdot G_b - k_{AA} \\cdot AA_b$$\nWhere:\n*   **$G_b$:** Basal Glucose (~90 mg/dl for CNT; ~125 mg/dl for T2D)\n*   **$I_b$:** Basal Insulin (~7.5 $\\mu$U/ml for CNT; ~14 $\\mu$U/ml for T2D)\n*   **$AA_b$:** Basal Amino Acids (~470 $\\mu$mol/L for CNT; ~530 $\\mu$mol/L for T2D)\n\n### **3. Virtual Population Values**\nFor the virtual population analysis (Section 3.2), the authors did not use a single fixed value but rather sampled $AA_b$ from a distribution to reflect physiological variability. The results of these individual simulations are summarized in **Figure 9** and **Table 1** (or the corresponding results text on **Page 11**), which show the distribution of insulin secretion parameters across the 200 virtual subjects.\n\n### **Summary of where to find these in the paper:**\n*   **Visual Data:** See **Figure 3 (Panel C)** on **Page 6** for the plots showing the average fasting and post-meal AA concentrations.\n*   **Mathematical Context:** See the **Methods (Section 2.1.1)** on **Page 3** for the definition of $AA_b$ in the $BR_I$ equation.\n*   **Reference Source:** The specific raw average numbers are derived from reference **[7]** (Karusheva et al., 2019, *AJCN*), which is explicitly credited in the text on **Page 4**.",
