        "text": "90,000 Daltons** (often cited as ~330–380 kDa in literature"
      }, {
        "text": ").\n*   This large structure is actually a **hexamer**—it is made of 6 major subunits that cling"
      }, {
        "text": " together to form a single massive globule.\n\n### 2. The \"Subunit\" Polypeptide (2"
      }, {
        "text": "1 kDa)\nThe **UniProt entry (P20780)** describes one of the individual polypeptide chains that make up"
      }, {
        "text": " that massive 380k complex.\n*   **Subunit cleavage:** Arachin subunits are synthesized as a single large"
      }, {
        "text": " precursor (around 60–70 kDa). This precursor is then \"clipped\" by enzymes into two pieces: an **acid"
      }, {
        "text": "ic chain** (approx. 35–45 kDa) and a **basic chain** (approx. "
      }, {
        "text": "20–25 kDa).\n*   **Identification:** The 21 kDa protein in your UniProt link"
      }, {
        "text": " is specifically the **basic subunit** of an Arachin protein (often associated with the allergen **Ara h 3**)."
      }, {
        "text": " \n*   **The Math:** To get from 21 kDa to 380 kDa:\n    *"
      }, {
        "text": "   1 basic chain (~21 kDa) + 1 acidic chain (~40 kDa) \u003d **~61"
      }, {
        "text": " kDa subunit**.\n    *   6 of these subunits ($61 \\times 6$) \u003d **~366 kDa"
      }, {
        "text": " total complex**.\n\n### 3. Comparison Table\n| Feature | Basha \u0026 Pancholy (1981)"
      }, {
        "text": " | UniProt (P20780) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n"
      }, {
        "text": "| **Value** | ~380,000 Daltons | 20,863 Dal"
      }, {
        "text": "tons (~21 kDa) |\n| **Perspective** | **Whole Complex** (Quaternary) | **Single"
      }, {
        "text": " Chain** (Primary/Secondary) |\n| **Analogy** | A six-pack of 12oz"
      }, {
        "text": " sodas. | A single aluminum can. |\n| **Measurement** | Gel Filtration (keeps the protein intact)."
      }, {
        "text": " | SDS-PAGE/Sequencing (breaks the protein into pieces). |\n\n### Summary\nThe 1981"
      }, {
        "text": " paper is looking at the **\"entire machine\"** as it functions in the seed, whereas the UniProt entry is"
      }, {
        "text": " a **\"part number\"** for one specific component of that machine. If you were to run the 380,"
      }, {
        "text": "000 Dalton protein through a denaturing gel (SDS-PAGE) today, it would break apart, and you would see"
      }, {
        "text": " a band at the 21 kDa mark mentioned in UniProt."
